			<h3 class="sub-title mb-3" id="changelog">Change Log</h3>
			<div class="copy stinger black mb-3">Content Updates</div>
			<p class="copy mb-3">Want these in a feed reader or a Discord server? Follow the <a href="rpg-feed.php">change log’s RSS feed</a>.</p>

			<div class="changelog-entries">
				<article class="blog-post">
					<p class="copy mb-3"><i>11/11/2026</i></p>
					<ul class="copy changelog-list mb-0">
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: Wealth. Characters start with a kit bought with Kit Points instead of money. Each item has a Kit Cost from Basic (free) to 5, and a character’s Wealth, from its Origin, Profession and Past, sets how many points it gets (3 + 2 per point of Wealth) and the dearest item it can start with. Wealthy backgrounds like Raised at Court or a Merchant Dynasty start with more and better gear; Gutter Trash starts lean. Points left over become starting cash in ERC or Luras when the character goes into play, and Wealth stays on the sheet. An AI Core gets its first chassis free, up to Kit Cost 3.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: AI Cores inhabit chassis. A chassis is an item: add one from Add item’s Chassis tab (free for now) and equip it, and its Physical stats, HP, Movement, Attacks and Traits become the AI Core’s. An AI Core can own several and inhabit one at a time; equipping another moves it there. Each chassis keeps its own HP, so one it leaves remembers its damage, and its core keeps its own 10 HP apart from them. Four chassis to start: Industrial Laborer, Courier Drone, Humanoid Service and Combat Walker, with the new Non-humanoid, Flight and Reinforced Conditions.</li>
						<li>Adventures: the Magic tab’s enchanted Items, Traveler’s Respite and the Amulet of the Seas, have − and + buttons on their stored MP, to track it as it’s spent and recharged.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article class="blog-post">
					<p class="copy mb-3"><i>11/10/2026</i></p>
					<ul class="copy changelog-list mb-0">
						<li>Character Creator: the Weapons Knowledge is gone, since it was far too broad. It’s off the Background Trait lists of the 12 Professions and 3 Pasts that had it.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article class="blog-post">
					<p class="copy mb-3"><i>11/9/2026</i></p>
					<ul class="copy changelog-list mb-0">
						<li>Setting: Murk Legs in Parazoology has a compact monster sheet with its Stats, HP, VP and SP, Massive Claws and Horrid Bite, and a permanent Rank 2 Dark Haze.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: new Illusion spell Dark Haze (Magic 4), which gives the Dark Haze Condition. Anyone trying to see a character with it needs an Intuition check of 10 per Rank, or they see only a dark, shimmering haze.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article class="blog-post">
					<p class="copy mb-3"><i>11/8/2026</i></p>
					<ul class="copy changelog-list mb-0">
						<li>Character Creator: Deathproof, Mindproof, Deathblade and Mindblade join the other proof and blade spells, with their Conditions (Magically Deathproof, Magically Mindproof, Withering Weapon and Maddening Weapon) and Deathproof and Mindproof Potions.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: Resistances and Damage Types fills out Death and Psychic damage. Death damage is rarely resisted, so Death Attacks hit hard but have no secondary effects; Psychic Attacks deal moderate damage and give Conditions.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: new Necromancy spells Grave Touch (Magic 2), Blight (Magic 5) and Stilled Heart (Magic 6), and a Mentalism spell, Mind Shatter (Magic 6, after Mind Spike). Wither now deals 6 Death per Rank.</li>
						<li>Adventures: the Magic tab has example magical Items under the rules for making them, with what each does and the MP an enchanted Item holds: three artifacts (Santar’s Sword of Rust, L’orian’s Erstwhile Companion and The Ring of the Wild Children), two enchanted Items (Traveler’s Respite and the Amulet of the Seas) and two potions (a Rank 3 Healing Potion and Firewalker’s Draught, with Flameproof and Haste at Rank 2).</li>
						<li>Mechanics: the Injuries tab shows Dress Wounds as an example Ability card under Healing, Medicine, and Regaining HP.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: Incidents has an Injuries tab. A Critical Hit that deals a quarter of a target’s HP can injure them on a failed Endurance check, with the injury set by the damage type (Broken Limb for Blunt, Scarred for Slashing, Organ Damage for Piercing, Severe Burn, Cursed, Mortis, Scrambled and Irradiated), alongside Deafened, Blinded and Paralyzed, and the Dress Wounds Ability (Intuition 2), whose Action gives the Bandaged Condition, doubling HP recovery for a day.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: the injury Conditions, Bandaged and the Dress Wounds Ability. Deafened is now a permanent injury; the Deafened that Thunderclap, Stormcraft, Electrified Weapon and the Thunder Flask give is now Temporarily Deafened, with the same effect for a minute.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: Items, Armor, and Effects’ Armor and Damage Types tab is now Resistances and Damage Types.</li>
						<li>Adventures: two more spell schools in the Magic tab, Restoration and Mentalism, for nine in all.</li>
						<li>Adventures: the Magic tab has the magic rules: Artifact Construction, Enchantment, Potion Making, and Reagents and the seven spell schools they come from.</li>
						<li>Adventures: Another World’s outline is now the Adventure Hook tab, beside new Magic and Monsters tabs. Isekai and the Kingdom of Dreft has Locations, Institutions and Religions tabs in place of its Politics, Religion, Military, Cultural Institutions and Magic sections, with every Dreftian location in Locations and a list of Dreft’s institutions, from the Crown and the noble houses to the trade guilds, hunting guilds and schools of magic, in Institutions. Building a Dreftian has Kinds, Backgrounds and Characters tabs, showing every Dreftian Kind, Profession and Past and every Isekai Origin (Dreft, Karsef, Sorellion and the Drovus Empire) from the Character Creator as its card, with what it grants and its Background list. Ark Tetra and Planar Exploration now has Ark Tetra’s entry from The Stars.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: five proof spells. Flameproof, Iceproof, Rustproof, Stormproof and Stoneproof give a character or item within 5 m 3 Heat, Cold, Corrosive, Electrical or Blunt resistance per Rank for 30 minutes per Rank, and each has a potion, drunk or poured over a character or object.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: five blade spells. Flameblade, Iceblade, Rustblade, Stormblade and Earthblade give a weapon within 5 m a new weapon Condition for 10 minutes per Rank, adding 3 Heat, 2 Cold, 2 Corrosive, 3 Electrical or 3 Blunt damage per Rank. Its hits give Burning, Frozen, Corroding or Deafened, and an Earthen Weapon knocks a target Prone on a Solid Hit or better.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: two new spells. Magical Replenishment gives another magic user up to 6 bonus MP per Rank from the caster’s own, which fade after 1 hour per Rank, and Mana Siphon is a ranged EMP Attack that drains 3 to 5 MP from the target, depending on the hit, into the caster, with any MP over the caster’s maximum kept as bonus MP for 1 hour per Rank. Mana Potions are now brewed at the brewer’s Rank in Magical Replenishment and give 6 bonus MP per Rank instead of restoring MP, and the Greater Mana Potion is gone.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: 13 new metamagic Abilities on the Magic tab. Simple Metamagic casts a spell a Rank higher for double the MP; Flamecraft, Icecraft, Stormcraft, Rustcraft and Stonecraft turn a spell’s Elemental damage into Heat, Cold, Electrical, Corrosive or Blunt for 1 more MP; Master Flamecraft, Master Icecraft, Master Stormcraft, Master Rustcraft and Master Stonecraft make spells of their damage type cheaper and stronger; and Master Mage and Archmage cut the MP every spell costs.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: Enchanting and Rune Carving give a flat +5 and are no longer Ranked, Artifact Repair needs Intuition instead of Memory, and Master Artificer’s requirements are lower and it gives Advantage on enchanting rolls.</li>
						<li>Mechanics, the Character Creator and Player Tools: Other Common Elemental Effects on the Damage Types tab are now Uncommon Elemental Effects, and EMP joins Radiation and Corrosive there instead of being an Elemental damage type.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: Inventor covers devices, machines and tools, including working out what an unfamiliar one is for. Field Medicine reduces Severe Bleeding, Unconscious, temporary blindness or a concussion, and Monster Hunter no longer gives +3 Defense against a marked quarry.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article class="blog-post">
					<p class="copy mb-3"><i>11/7/2026</i></p>
					<ul class="copy changelog-list mb-0">
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: a new Grenadier Ability, which gives the Lob Action: throwing a grenade or flask at a spot the character can’t see.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: a new Frozen Condition, -1 Priority, Defense and Attack Rolls per Rank. Hoarfrost, the Frost Flask and Frost Breath give it.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: spells and flasks that give a ranked Condition say they give one Rank of it, like Fireball’s Burning. Ranked Conditions that wear off now lose a Rank at a time, like Frozen: every hour for Magical Strength, every combat Round or 10 seconds for Slowed, and every three combat Rounds or 30 seconds for Burning and Corroding.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: 23 new Circumstances. Memberships come in two tiers, a Member and a Senior Member, for the Explorers’ Lodge (Explorers’ Lodge Membership is now Member of the Explorers’ Lodge), the Monster Hunter Guild, the Mages College of Dreft and the thieves’ guilds, plus a Merchant Clan Member and Elder. Others include Tetra Frontiers Co. Employee, Switch Port Transit Pass, Diplomatic Immunity, Bureau Credentials, Knighted in Dreft, Royal Warrant, Caravan Charter, Research Grant, Owed a Favor, Heavy Debts, Wanted in Dreft and Exiled from Dreft.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: Knowledges reviewed. Geography, History, Legal Systems, Southeast Asia, Dead Languages and Archives and Libraries are gone as too broad or too specific; packages that offered History offer Local History instead. Pedagogy is now Education. Criminal Underworld, Heraldry and Navigation ask where the character knows them. Fourteen Knowledges need less, mostly Memory 3 in place of 4, like Physics, Pharmacology and Contract Law, and Religions of Isekai and of the Settled Systems now need Empathy 2.</li>
						<li>Mechanics, the Character Creator and Player Tools: the Acidic/Corrosive damage type is now just Corrosive, on the Damage Types tab, item resistances like the Hazmat Suit’s, Acid Spray and the Corroding Condition. Corrosive effects give objects the Corroding Condition.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: Natural Breath Weapon now grants the Breath Weapon natural weapon (1 Blunt + Physical, 10 m range, 3 m area, once every 3 Rounds), and adds 2 to its damage per Rank. Fire Breath, Frost Breath and Acid Breath turn its damage to Heat, Cold or Corrosive, with a Condition on a Devastating Hit or better. A character takes only one of them.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: 37 potions. Most are brewed at the Rank of the spell they come from: drink one, like a Strength Potion, Potion of Haste or Healing Potion, for the spell’s effect, or throw a flask, like an Explosive Flask or Acid Flask, and the spell goes off where it breaks. The Mana Potion restores 6 MP and the Greater Mana Potion 12. Spells with a potion are marked Potion.</li>
						<li>Mechanics and the Character Creator: Skills that let a character do the basics without a Skill Check (crafts, art, performance, cooking, riding, climbing, jumping and more) add Rank *5 instead of Rank *10. Interrogation, Hazard Assessment and Fancy Footwork have new effects, and Unconscious says how a character wakes up.</li>
						<li>The Character Creator: new Field Medicine Ability and High Morale Condition. Bookkeeping, Brokering, Active Listening and Cultural Fluency are gone.</li>
						<li>The Character Creator: Sprinter is an Ability with a Sprint Action (+10 m moving in a straight line). Fine Print now covers loopholes too, so Loophole Finder is gone, and 14 more Skills have broader or clearer effects, among them Diplomacy, Handler, Procurement, Contortionist, Data Analysis and the hacking Skills.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article class="blog-post">
					<p class="copy mb-3"><i>11/6/2026</i></p>
					<ul class="copy changelog-list mb-0">
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: eleven new Traits for smugglers and street folk. Skills: Hidden Holds, Checkpoint Nerve, Greasing Palms, Fence, Dock Rat, Running Dark, Route Memory and Sizing Up. Abilities: Knife Work, Bolt and Sh!t Talk. The Smuggler’s Background list adds Hidden Holds, Checkpoint Nerve, Greasing Palms, Fence and Running Dark. On character sheets, Abilities and Skills share their space equally until the Abilities fit two columns.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: Edwin spends eleven of his picks on new Traits: Knife Work, Bolt and Sh!t Talk (Abilities), and Dock Rat, Route Memory, Sizing Up, Hidden Holds, Checkpoint Nerve, Greasing Palms, Fence and Running Dark (Skills). The last five are on the Smuggler’s Background list now, and he has one Background pick left.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: Edwin Humble, the Sample Character Sheet’s character, is Level 6. His new core point went into Social (now 3), with 1 each into Empathy, Persuasion and Demeanor, so his VP is 12 and he has 12 picks available (6 Universal, 6 Background).</li>
						<li>Mechanics: the Sample Character Sheet’s Traits use the creator’s current wording. Concealment, Sleight of Hand, Haggler, Streetwise, Smooth Talker, Schemer, Pilot: Truck, Appraisal and Cargo Handling have their effects instead of placeholders, and the Wielder skills’ effects are bulleted, as in the creator.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: new combat Abilities in the same vein as Boxing and Expert Boxer. Swordsman gives a Riposte Action, an Attack back in the next Priority step after a miss, and its Mastery, Expert Swordsman, a Flurry of two sword Attacks and Advantage with swords. Archer gives an Aimed Shot at +4 that costs 6 Priority for the Round, and Expert Archer a two-arrow Volley and Advantage with bows and crossbows. Knight, built on Rider, gives a mounted Charge. Barbarian spends 1 VP to gain the new Rage Condition, which doubles Attack damage, gives -10 to Social and Mental rolls, and ends after any turn without an Attack. Hunter, built on Tracker, has the player write in what counts as their quarry, and Mark Quarry spends 1 SP and a Knowledge check for +3 to Attack Rolls against it for the Incident. Monster Hunter is now an Ability built on Hunter, adding +3 Defense against a marked quarry; Slayer still sits above it. Counterpuncher’s Attack back also comes in the next Priority step.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: Traits that give a character something new to do are now Abilities. Boxing (Haymaker and Uppercut), Martial Artist (Roundhouse Kick) and Counterpuncher (an Attack back after a miss) move from Skills.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: Edwin Humble spends three banked picks on new Skills from his smuggling runs: Cover Identity, Poker Face and Procurement, leaving nine picks available.</li>
						<li>Mechanics and Character Creator: Skills are now what a character is good at and the modifiers they get for it, and Abilities are what a character actively decides to use. Con Man, Eagle Eye, Mental Fortitude, Sculpted, Trail Runner, Gladiator, Capable Student and Knowledge Sponge become Skills; Rally, Grappler, Takedown, Disarm and Weak Point become Abilities; Long in the Tooth and Magic Access move to Other. The Traits page’s Skill and Ability examples and Edwin’s sample sheet follow.</li>
						<li>Mechanics and Character Creator: natural weapons. Every character can Attack with Fists and Kick, which deal 1 Blunt + Power. Boxing grants Haymaker and Uppercut, and the new Expert Boxer Ability grants Superman Punch; Martial Artist grants Roundhouse Kick, and the new Martial Arts Master Ability grants Bicycle Kick and Five Fingered Palm of Death. Brawler is now a Skill adding 1 Blunt damage per Rank to natural weapons, in place of its Unarmed Strike Action, and a knockout punch can give the new Unconscious Condition.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: five new Skills built on punches and kicks: Hard Puncher and Shin Training add Blunt damage per Rank to punches and kicks (Shin Training also hardens the legs), Iron Jaw helps resist being knocked Unconscious, Boxer’s Defense adds +3 Defense against punches, and Fancy Footwork, a Mastery of Footwork, adds 2 m of Movement and Advantage on dodging.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: Stat Types has a new Special Stats section, using Magic as the example: who can spend points in one, how its points become resource points instead of focus Stats, and how Traits built on it list it as a requirement. Stat-Based Resources opens with how resources work, adds regain rates for HP, VP and SP, and Mana Points becomes Special Stat Points, which regain 3 per hour.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: every character now has the Magic tab when picking Traits. Spells and other Traits that need Magic stay out of reach until a character can level it, while Magic-related Traits with no Magic requirement, like Relic Handling and Knowledge: Magic on Isekai, are open to anyone who meets their stats. Knowledge: Enchantment, Artifact Identification, Knowledge: Magical Artifacts and Knowledge: Runecraft join the Magic tab.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: 15 new spells: Cleanse, Staunch, Detect Magic, Fog Cloud, Ice Lance, Earthen Spike, Telekinesis, Darkness, Daze, Speak with Animals, Wall of Stone, Banish Spirit, Chain Lightning, Greater Heal and Meteor.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: 50 more Skills, ten each for leadership and command, espionage and intelligence, faith, ritual and spirits, salvage, demolition and heavy industry, and scholarship and teaching. Rally ends Frightened on allies who can hear, and Battlefield Commander gives them +1 Priority.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: 14 more Knowledges to go with them, including Rhetoric, Intelligence Tradecraft, Religions of Isekai, Spirits and the Dead, Explosives, Dead Languages and Pedagogy.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: 100 new Skills, ten each for martial arts and boxing, athletics, invention and planar exploration, potions and magical artifacts, hacking, piloting, negotiation and contracts, diplomacy, field medicine, and monsters and extraplanar beings. Brawler gives an Unarmed Strike Action, and Grappler, Takedown and Disarm give Actions of their own.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: 15 new Knowledges to go with them, including Martial Arts, Anatomy, Switch Gates, Enchantment, Contract Law, Combat Medicine and Extraplanar Threats.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: Ambusher, Appraisal, Vigilance and 24 other Skills now have their effects and minimum stats. Shield Wall is now an Ability with a Shieldwall Action, which gives every ally holding a shield and Defending beside you +4 Defense.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article class="blog-post">
					<p class="copy mb-3"><i>11/5/2026</i></p>
					<ul class="copy changelog-list mb-0">
						<li>Character Creator: Magic Access’s effect now just says the character can level up the Magic core stat.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: Magical Heritage is a Condition rather than an Ability.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: 35 magic Abilities join the Magic list, each giving a Cast Action, among them Fireball, Lightning, Hoarfrost, Heal, Mending, Skin of Stone, Invisibility, Haste, Sleep, Charm, Dispel Magic and Blink, with Magic minimums from 1 to 4. The Conditions they give come too, like Burning, Corroding, Stone Skin, Shielded, Prone, Frightened, Asleep and Charmed. Long Toothed comes from Long in the Tooth, Hard Shell has no Stat minimum, and AI Cores can take Cybernetic Intelligence as a Background Trait.</li>
						<li>Sorcerous is gone, since Magic Access does its job. Its card is off the Traits page’s Background-Only examples.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: Conditions no longer carry Stat requirements. In Traits’ Background-Only examples, Long Toothed comes from a new Background Ability, Long in the Tooth, which holds its requirements (Power 10, Endurance 5, Demeanor 5, Middle Aged or Older), and Hard Shell drops its Endurance 5. Character Creator: Cybernetic Intelligence is on every AI Core’s Background Trait list.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: in Items, each Item Type on the Item Types tab now has an example Item card from the Character Creator under its description: Power Armor (Wearables), a Grappling Hook (Equipment), a Longbow (Weapons), a Tent (Structures), a Rowboat (Vehicles), a Pack Animal (Animals) and Sling Stones (Misc). Item cards can show Radiation resistance.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: Edwin carries three more items from the Character Creator: an equipped Pistol (7 Piercing), a Disguise Kit and a Comm Unit. He takes Wielder: Pistol with one of his universal picks, and Eagle Eye, a Conveyed Ability, came to him in play with one of his banked picks, leaving 12 picks available. His Cash is off the sheet; his Wealth stays.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: the Sample Character Sheet opens with Building a Character, from the Mechanics Doc, in place of the Musings tab. It covers the four Backgrounds, starting Stats and Traits, how to read the sheet, and where Edwin’s 25 focus points went. The backgrounds Edwin uses sit beside it as cards, like the Character Creator’s, each with its Bonus, Grants, Choose and Background list as badges, and the section’s tab box is gone.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: Stats and Example Stats revised from the Mechanics Doc. Magic is now one of the Special Stats, extra core Stats that a Trait opens, with no focus Stats and their own resource. The 20-point cap covers Special Stats, and some Kinds set lower maximums. The Example Stats copy is regrouped around the Human’s Generalist and Unexceptional Traits and what its Physical build can and can’t do.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: the Explaining Traits intro revised from the Mechanics Doc. It’s regrouped into a Trait’s category and type, how Traits are gained, banking, temporary Traits, and the four kinds of requirements (Stats, Prerequisite Traits, Training and Role-playing), which Background packages skip. The first example Knowledge is Local History, as its text already described, and Capable Student loses its stray parentheses.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: What Is a Skill Check? and Requesting Competence revised from the Mechanics Doc. Skill Checks now explain the roll first, then core and complex checks, target values, success as a gradient and repeat attempts. Requesting Competence says the GM can allow or deny it and decides its outcome.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article class="blog-post">
					<p class="copy mb-3"><i>11/4/2026</i></p>
					<ul class="copy changelog-list mb-0">
						<li>Wielder Traits give +3 to Attack Rolls made with their weapon, at any Rank. Their Rank × 5 bonus still applies only to Skill Checks. This covers every Wielder Trait in the Character Creator and Player Tools, and the Wielder: Longsword and Wielder: Musket examples in Explaining Traits.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: shields resist damage and add to Defense when Defending: Buckler +2, Wooden Shield +4, Tower Shield +6, Ballistic Shield +5.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: a new Flat-Footed Condition gives −1 Priority and −1 to Attack Rolls through the following combat Round.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: the sheet shows the character’s Movement after HP, VP and SP: 10 m for every Kind but the bodiless AI Core.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: in Incidents, Damage notes that a weapon with a choice of damage types, like the Longsword’s 6 Slashing / 4 Piercing, makes the player choose which type an Attack deals. The damage example now uses a Spear against chainmail.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: a new Incidents section, between Skill Checks and Items, sets the rules for combat and other tense scenes: Rounds and Priority Order, the basic Actions, Movement, Attacking with hit and miss Severities, Defenses and Defending, Melee and Ranged Attacks with Line of Sight and Cover, Area of Effect and Thrown weapons, Damage, and Role-Playing Actions.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: the Sample Character Sheet shows Edwin’s Movement, 10 m, beside his HP, VP and SP.</li>
						<li>The Stars: every star system lists an estimated population, from 13 billion in the Sol System and 50 million around Alpha Centauri to 1.1 million at YZ Ceti. The Sol System’s Nationalities is a See Nations link that opens the Setting’s Nations tab.</li>
						<li>The Stars: Water Gates joins the Technology tab under Fuel Gates, as a placeholder for now.</li>
						<li>The Stars: most star systems now list the nations present there, and each system’s Confirmed Planets is a plain list of planet names. The Sol System heads the list.</li>
						<li>The Stars: the Systems tab lists twelve nearby star systems, from Alpha Centauri to YZ Ceti, each with its distance in light-years and its known planets. The rest of each entry is a placeholder for now.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article class="blog-post">
					<p class="copy mb-3"><i>11/3/2026</i></p>
					<ul class="copy changelog-list mb-0">
						<li>Character Creator: AI Cores now hold the Mechanical Condition from their Kind, shown with their Traits, so they’re harmed by EMP damage and usually immune to Death damage.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: armor and clothing Items show how much they resist, like 3 Blunt, 4 Slashing, 2 Piercing (head) for the Steel Helm, and 14 new armors are in: Leather Jacket, Power Armor, Hide Armor, Brigandine, Padded Coif, Buckler, Tower Shield, Warded Robes, Plate Carrier, Ballistic Shield, Turnout Gear, Rad Suit, Faraday Shroud and Combat Voidsuit.</li>
						<li>Character Creator and Player Tools: weapons show how much damage they deal, like 7 Slashing for the War Axe. Damage separated by commas is all dealt at once, and a slash between options, like the Longsword’s 6 Slashing / 4 Piercing, means the player picks one. Nine new weapons are in: Rapier, Hand Axe, Flail, Maul, Combat Knife, Revolver, Submachine Gun, Taser and Incendiary Grenade.</li>
						<li>The Stars: the Stations and Systems tabs now hold their first entries, Antiliuna and Alpha Centauri, as placeholders laid out like the Arks.</li>
						<li>Added the five biomedical firms from the Biology tab to the Corporations tab: Blue Frontier, Jensen &amp; Kim, Lunar Gentech, Mumbai Ecological Solutions, and Stohnroth.</li>
						<li>Rebirth of Science: the Biology tab’s Overview is expanded with human enhancement, the trade in parabiological samples, and the top five biomedical firms, and its History is written, from the advances of the 21st century to the fall of the gene-tailored elite after the Second Major AI Panic.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article class="blog-post">
					<p class="copy mb-3"><i>11/2/2026</i></p>
					<ul class="copy changelog-list mb-0">
						<li>Mechanics: Edwin Humble’s Sample Character Sheet now comes from the Character Creator’s content: The American Empire: Earth, Smuggler and Gutter Trash, with the creator’s Trait cards (effect and source) and a legal set of picks.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: revised wording across Explaining Traits, Skill Checks, Items, Armor, and Effects, and the Sample Character Sheet, from the Mechanics Doc. Language Traits say a character can speak and understand a language, Expert Pilot needs any Pilot Trait, Wielder Traits cover using a weapon as well as maintaining it, Dead is no longer an (Injury), and Possessed by a Spirit lists Persuasion 9.</li>
						<li>Game terms are capitalized across Strange Frontiers and the Character Creator: Trait, Stat, Level, Rank, Item, Equipment, Advantage, Competence, Roll Modifier, Universal and Background, the Item categories and damage types, Kind names, and the Settled Systems. Trait types are written in parentheses, like (Injury).</li>
						<li>Explaining Stats: revised wording from the Mechanics Doc. Stats now represent a character’s physical, social and mental limitations, HP is 10 plus one for each Physical focus point, a maxed-out Human is roughly 20x (not 30x) as tough as a starting one, and Logic gains a line on reasoning through problems given time.</li>
						<li>The Stars: revised wording for the Starships overview, most ship classes (cutters, dreadnoughts, miners, stellar carriers and more), Arks and Tetra, from the Doc. Tetra was first laid down in 2163, not 2165.</li>
						<li>Space suits are “voidsuits” throughout, including the Voidsuit in Example Items, and ship classes are lowercase mid-sentence (Arks stay capitalized).</li>
						<li>Rebirth of Science: revised wording across Paraphysics, Artificial Intelligence, Biology, Cybernetics and Robotics, from the Doc. A typical AI Core is now a 15 cm (6-inch) ball.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: the stock Items are in. Characters the AI builds start with Items that fit their description and work, from their own plane. Player Tools’ assistant knows them too.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article class="blog-post">
					<p class="copy mb-3"><i>10/30/2026</i></p>
					<ul class="copy changelog-list mb-0">
						<li>Rebirth of Science: the introduction, Switch Gates, Lorentz Field Generators and Aether Sails text is revised. Interstellar travel is now a recent frontier: the first experimental Lorentz field generators are tested in 2160, and New Canaan, the first interstellar colony, is founded by the first Ark in 2190, beginning interstellar expansion. Interdimensional colonization begins in 2116, and the End of Science runs from 2070 to 2120. Nearly a dozen star systems now have populations of at least 1 million, and Leviathan’s prototype water gate was installed on a research station in the outer Sol System. The timeline is updated to match.</li>
						<li>Parabiology: the subtitle is now “Life Among the Planes,” the introduction text is revised, and the Isek, Tatot and Guwain entries replace “coming soon” with notes on their lives and societies.</li>
						<li>“Lodge” is capitalized wherever it means the Explorers’ Lodge.</li>
						<li>Mechanics: the placeholder subtitles are replaced: Explaining Stats is “Core and Focus,” Explaining Traits “Who and What a Character Is,” Skill Checks “Rolls, Modifiers, and Outcomes,” Items, Armor, and Effects “Outfitting a Character,” and the Sample Character Sheet “Putting It All Together.”</li>
						<li>Items: new Equipment cards, the Item counterpart to Trait cards, showing an Item’s category, plane, description and value. Example Items on the Items page shows them for Weapons, Wearables, Equipment, Vehicles and animals, and Misc Items, with one value per item: in Dreft’s Luras for Items from Isekai, and in ERC for everything else.</li>
						<li>Items: Weapons and Vehicles no longer require a Trait. Anyone can use them, but without a related Trait, such as a Wielder or Pilot skill, a character takes a penalty for unfamiliarity.</li>
						<li>Character Creator: 19 new Wielder skills covering weapon families from daggers, spears, polearms, bows, crossbows and slings to shotguns, machine guns, grenades, flamethrowers and missile launchers, on the Background Trait lists of the soldiers, guards, hunters and knights who would use them.</li>
						<li>Known Planes: Isekai’s population reads ~220 million native (est.) + ~12,000 Earth baseline, and its Paraphysics, Geography and History text is revised. In The Account of the Team’s Trouble, the team leader is now Vikram Archest.</li>
						<li>Humanity’s home system is the Sol System everywhere on the site and in the Character Creator, in place of “Solar System,” “solar system” and “Sol system.”</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
